# MRBD UI Kit Rules

You are building for the Meta Ray-Ban Display — a 600×600 additive display in smart glasses. Use the `mrbd-ui-kit` package.

## Critical Constraints
- NEVER use `#FFFFFF` or pure white — causes ghosting. Use `text-mrbd-text`.
- NEVER use `drop-shadow` or `box-shadow` for decoration — looks like dirt. Use `shadow-mrbd-glow-*`.
- NEVER use `font-weight` below 500 — illegible on additive display.
- ALWAYS wrap MRBD UI in `<DisplayRoot>`.
- ALWAYS give every `<Focusable>`, `<Button>`, and nav item a unique `id`.

## Imports
```typescript
// Components + hooks
import { DisplayRoot, Text, Box, Stack, Icon, Focusable, Button, NavigationBar, LoadingIndicator, useDpad, useFocusManager, useIsMRBD } from 'mrbd-ui-kit';

// Server detection
import { isMRBD, isMRBDFromHeaders } from 'mrbd-ui-kit/server';

// Next.js RSC detection
import { isMRBDServer } from 'mrbd-ui-kit/next';
```

## CSS Setup
```css
@import "tailwindcss";
@import "mrbd-ui-kit/css/theme";
@import "mrbd-ui-kit/css/base";
```

For full API reference, read `AGENTS.md` at the repository root.
